        "content_section_GLa7AN": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Vendor",
            "title": "Clause 1 – Identity of the vendor",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>You buy from KARMICA BV, a Belgian company in Bruges.</strong></p><p>The webshop <a href=\"https://www.karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">karmicare.com</a> and its checkout subdomains are operated by:<br/><br/><strong>KARMICA BV</strong> (trading as <strong>KARMICARE</strong>), Vizierstraat 28, 8000 Bruges, Belgium · Enterprise number (KBO/BCE) 0676.972.896 · VAT BE 0676.972.896 · RPR Enterprise Court of Ghent, division Bruges · EORI BE0676972896 · Belfius Bank, IBAN BE73 0689 0664 2960, BIC GKCCBEBB · <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a></p>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_g6nYeY": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Scope",
            "title": "Clause 2 – Applicability and international scope",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>These terms apply to every order and plan you place on karmicare.com.</strong></p><ol><li>These General Terms and Conditions (“Terms”) apply to all offers, orders, contracts of sale and plan agreements concluded via our website between KARMICA BV (“we”, “us”, “vendor”) and any purchaser (“you”, “customer”).</li><li>A <strong>“Consumer”</strong> is any natural person acting for purposes outside their trade, business, craft or profession (Article I.1, 2° of the Belgian Code of Economic Law, WER). If you order as a dental professional, clinic or reseller, specific B2B conditions apply in addition to these Terms.</li><li><strong>Territorial scope:</strong> we ship to consumers in Belgium, the Netherlands, Luxembourg, France, Germany, Austria, Denmark, Sweden, Finland, Spain, Portugal, Italy, Greece, Ireland, Iceland, Norway, Switzerland, the United Kingdom, the United States, Canada, Australia, New Zealand, Singapore, Japan and other countries listed at checkout. We may decline orders to territories where shipping or customs restrictions make delivery unfeasible.</li><li><strong>Non-discrimination and geo-blocking (Regulation (EU) 2018/302):</strong> we do not apply discriminatory conditions or geo-blocking based on the nationality, place of residence or place of establishment of EU customers.</li><li><strong>Age:</strong> by placing an order, you confirm that you are at least 18 years old or have the consent of a parent or legal guardian.</li><li><strong>Access to these Terms:</strong> these Terms are always available at <a href=\"https://www.karmicare.com/en/pages/terms-and-conditions\" target=\"_blank\">karmicare.com/en/pages/terms-and-conditions</a> and are provided to you on a durable, printable medium with your order confirmation.</li></ol>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_iDEfUH": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Offers and contract",
            "title": "Clause 3 – Product classification, offers and contract formation",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Awake and Asleep are cosmetics, not medicines. Your order becomes a contract once we confirm it by email.</strong></p><ol><li><strong>EU cosmetic status: </strong>KARMICARE products (including our oral care systems, personal hygiene formulations and related accessories) are classified and notified as cosmetics under Regulation (EC) No 1223/2009 and manufactured under Good Manufacturing Practices (ISO 22716). They are not medicinal products or medical devices. Product descriptions, biorhythmic formulations and ingredient information describe cosmetic hygiene properties, enamel support and daily care, and are not medical diagnoses, treatments or cures.</li><li><strong>Offers:</strong> product descriptions, formulations and illustrations on our website are presented as precisely as possible. Minor variations in packaging or shade are not a defect. Obvious errors in prices or descriptions do not bind KARMICA BV.</li><li><strong>Contract formation:</strong> selecting products and completing checkout is an offer to buy. As Belgian and EU consumer law requires, our final order button is clearly labelled “Pay now” or with equivalent wording. The contract is concluded when we send you an automated order confirmation email with your order summary, delivery details and a copy of these Terms.</li></ol>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_FcEDdA": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Withdrawal and refunds",
            "title": "Clause 4 – Withdrawal, 60-day guarantee and refunds",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Changed your mind about a one-time order? You have 14 days. On the 60-Day plan or the Karmicare Year, you have 60 days to live the ritual and still get a full refund.</strong></p><p>KARMICARE applies differentiated, customer-first refund policies:<br/><br/><strong>4.1 One-time orders (Try once): 14-day statutory withdrawal and refund</strong></p><ol><li><strong>14-day cooling-off period: </strong>for one-time purchases, you have the statutory right to withdraw from the contract and request a full refund within <strong>14 calendar days</strong> of physical delivery (Article VI.47 WER).</li><li><strong>Reimbursement: </strong>if you withdraw in line with this clause, we reimburse all payments received from you, including standard delivery charges, within<strong> 14 calendar days </strong>of receiving the returned unopened goods or proof of return shipment.</li><li><strong>Same payment method: </strong>we reimburse via the <strong>same payment method</strong> you used (for example card via Stripe, PayPal, Bancontact or iDEAL). We never substitute a voucher unless you expressly ask for one.</li></ol><p><strong>4.2 60-Day plan and Karmicare Year: 60-day satisfaction guarantee</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Extended guarantee: </strong>on the <strong>60-Day plan</strong> or the <strong>Karmicare Year</strong>, KARMICARE provides an extended commercial <strong>60-calendar-day satisfaction guarantee,</strong> unless a specific promotional or product page states otherwise.</li><li><strong>Evaluation period:</strong> because an effective oral care habit takes consistent daily practice, you have <strong>60 calendar days from delivery</strong> to experience and evaluate Awake and Asleep.</li><li><strong>Refund process: </strong>if within those 60 days you are not satisfied with your ritual or your experience, notify our customer care at <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a>. We refund your initial plan order in full within <strong>14 calendar days</strong> of your request.</li><li><strong>Same payment method: </strong>plan refunds go back to the <strong>same payment method</strong> you used at checkout.</li></ol><p><strong>4.3 Packaging notice: airless pump and first-use priming</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Hermetic airless packaging: </strong>where KARMICARE formulas come in airless packaging, the pump creates a continuous vacuum that protects the active formulation (nHAp, botanical extracts, nootropics) from air, oxidation and bacterial contamination without harsh chemical preservatives.</li><li><strong>Unprimed factory state:</strong> the pumps are not pre-pumped in our manufacturing facility. On delivery, the internal vacuum chamber is hermetically sealed and unprimed.</li><li><strong>First-use priming (3 to 10 pumps):</strong> on first use, press the pump head firmly 3 to 10 times to activate the piston, clear the air chamber and draw the formula into the nozzle. This is normal for unprimed airless packaging.</li><li><strong>Hygiene seal exemption (Art. VI.53, 5° WER / Art. 16(e) Directive 2011/83/EU):</strong> sealed goods that are not suitable for return for health protection or hygiene reasons and were unsealed after delivery are exempt from the right of withdrawal. For <strong>one-time orders</strong>, an unprimed bottle with intact tamper-evident packaging can be returned within 14 calendar days; once primed, it counts as unsealed for intimate personal hygiene and the statutory right of return for that unit ends. On the<strong> 60-Day plan and the Karmicare Year,</strong> the 60-day satisfaction guarantee (clause 4.2) still applies after priming.</li></ol><p><strong>4.4 How to request a refund or return</strong></p><p><strong>Prices include VAT. Outside the EU, local import duties may apply.</strong></p><ol><li><strong>All-inclusive consumer prices:</strong> for deliveries within the European Union, all prices include Belgian VAT, or the VAT rate of your EU country through the EU One-Stop Shop (OSS).</li><li><strong>Shipping charges: </strong>shipping rates, express fees and free-shipping thresholds are shown in your cart and on the final checkout page before payment.</li><li><strong>Deliveries outside the EU (for example the UK, US, Canada and Australia):</strong> these may be subject to local import taxes, customs duties and clearance fees charged in your country. Unless checkout marks the order as Delivered Duty Paid (DDP), these charges are yours.</li><li><strong>Price reductions (Omnibus Directive):</strong> under Article VI.19/1 WER, when we advertise a price reduction, the reference price is the<strong> lowest price KARMICARE applied for that product in the 30 calendar days before the promotion.</strong></li></ol>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_xKcNPj": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Prices and taxes",
            "title": "Clause 5 – Prices, taxes, customs and discounts",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Prices include VAT. Outside the EU, local import duties may apply.</strong></p><ol><li><strong>All-inclusive consumer prices:</strong> for deliveries within the European Union, all prices include Belgian VAT, or the VAT rate of your EU country through the EU One-Stop Shop (OSS).</li><li><strong>Shipping charges: </strong>shipping rates, express fees and free-shipping thresholds are shown in your cart and on the final checkout page before payment.</li><li><strong>Deliveries outside the EU (for example the UK, US, Canada and Australia): </strong>these may be subject to local import taxes, customs duties and clearance fees charged in your country. Unless checkout marks the order as Delivered Duty Paid (DDP), these charges are yours.</li><li><strong>Price reductions (Omnibus Directive): </strong>under Article VI.19/1 WER, when we advertise a price reduction, the reference price is the <strong>lowest price KARMICARE applied for that product in the 30 calendar days before the promotion.</strong></li></ol>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_rnPj6g": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Payment",
            "title": "Clause 6 – Payment methods and security",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>You pay through certified payment providers. We never see or store your full card details.</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Accepted methods: </strong>Bancontact / Payconiq, iDEAL, credit and debit cards (Visa, Mastercard, American Express, Maestro), Apple Pay, Google Pay, Shop Pay and PayPal.</li><li><strong>Security and encryption: </strong>payments are encrypted with TLS and processed by PCI-DSS Level 1 certified providers (<strong>Stripe Payments Europe Ltd.</strong> and <strong>PayPal (Europe) S.à r.l.</strong>). KARMICA BV never stores, processes or has access to your full card details.</li><li><strong>Strong customer authentication: </strong>under the revised Payment Services Directive (PSD2), online card payments use 3D Secure two-factor authentication.</li></ol>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_EAKJLC": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Warranty",
            "title": "Clause 7 – Legal guarantee of conformity",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>A faulty pump, a defective formula or a broken brush is covered for two years. Using up a formula is not a defect.</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Legal framework:</strong> European consumers have a legal guarantee of conformity under Articles 1649bis to 1649octies of the Belgian Civil Code and Book VI WER, transposing Directive (EU) 2019/771 (Law of 20 March 2022).</li><li><strong>Consumable oral care (nature of the goods):</strong> under <strong>Article 1649quater, §4 of the Belgian Civil Code</strong>, the guarantee applies taking into account the nature of the goods. KARMICARE formulas are <strong>consumable cosmetic goods</strong> designed for an intended cycle of daily use (for example 30 to 60 days, depending on volume and frequency). The guarantee does not mean a formula lasts two years once opened. Normal depletion, natural bristle wear, or use beyond the Period After Opening (PAO) or minimum durability date is not a lack of conformity.</li><li><strong>What is covered:</strong> latent manufacturing defects and mechanical non-conformities present at or arising from delivery: failure, jamming or breakage of the airless pump while formula remains inside under normal use; formulation defects such as premature separation, contamination, abnormal discolouration or instability before the expiry date or PAO when stored as recommended; defective seals, leaking containers or structural defects in toothbrush handles or floss dispensers.</li><li><strong>Remedies:</strong> for a verified manufacturing or packaging defect, KARMICARE provides a <strong>free replacement</strong> of the defective unit (or a replacement bottle or pump). If replacement is impossible or disproportionate, you are entitled to a proportionate price reduction, or to end the contract with a full refund.</li><li><strong>Notification: </strong>tell us within <strong>two months</strong> of discovering a lack of conformity (Art. 1649quater, §2 Belgian Civil Code) by emailing <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a> with your order number, a description, and photos or a video of the defect.</li><li><strong>Exclusions:</strong> normal depletion of the formula; natural wear of toothbrush bristles; damage from improper storage (extreme temperatures, direct sunlight, moisture or tampering with the bottle); use after the PAO or expiry date.</li></ol><p><strong>Examples</strong></p>",
            "block_content": "<p><strong>Normal product depletion: excluded</strong> Example: asking for a replacement because the formula has been used up.<br/><strong>Why: </strong>consumable cosmetics are designed to be used up; normal exhaustion fulfils the contract.</p><p><strong>Normal bristle wear: excluded</strong> Example: bristles splaying or softening after 2–3 months of daily brushing.<br/><strong>Why: </strong>routine wear and tear; dentists recommend replacing a toothbrush every 2–3 months.</p><p><strong>Expired Period After Opening (PAO): excluded</strong> Example: a bottle opened 18 months ago dries out.<br/><strong>Why: </strong>stability is certified only within the indicated PAO.</p><p><strong>Improper storage: excluded</strong> Example: a bottle left on a radiator or in a hot car separates.<br/><strong>Why: </strong>heat damage caused by storage against the storage guidelines.</p><p><strong>Airless pump failure: covered</strong> Example: the piston jams or the head breaks in week 2 under normal use while formula remains inside.<br/><strong>Remedy: </strong>free replacement unit.</p><p><strong>Formulation or batch defect: covered</strong> Example: curdled, separated or discoloured formula on first use.<br/><strong>Remedy:</strong> free replacement or full refund.</p><p><strong>Unopened stock within shelf life: covered</strong> Example: a properly stored, unopened plan bottle goes bad before its printed expiry date.<br/><strong>Remedy:</strong> replacement.</p><p><strong>Structural toothbrush or floss defect: covered</strong> Example: a handle snaps on day 4 or bristles shed on first use.<br/><strong>Remedy:</strong> replacement.</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_section_dGmgBJ": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Delivery",
            "title": "Clause 8 – Delivery and transfer of risk",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Until your parcel is in your hands, it is our responsibility.</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Transfer of risk (Art. VI.44 WER):</strong> the risk of loss, theft or damage in transit stays with KARMICA BV until you, or a third party you designate (other than the carrier), take physical possession. You bear no financial risk for parcels lost or damaged in transit.</li><li><strong>Delivery address: </strong>we deliver to the shipping address in your order. Please make sure it is complete and correct.</li><li><strong>Delivery windows:</strong> Belgium and the Netherlands 1–3 business days; European Union and United Kingdom 2–5 business days; North America (US, CA) 4–8 business days; rest of the world 6–12 business days.</li><li><strong>Delays:</strong> if delivery is later than the agreed window (or than 30 days after the contract when no date was agreed), you can ask for delivery within an additional reasonable period. If we still fail to deliver, you can end the contract and receive a full refund of everything you paid within <strong>14 calendar days</strong> of termination.</li></ol>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_CDtWCV": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Plans",
            "title": "Clause 9 – Plans and recurring deliveries",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>No lock-in. Pause, skip, change or cancel your plan at any time before the renewal cut-off.</strong></p><p>KARMICARE offers optional, flexible plans for the recurring replenishment of formulas and replacement accessories.</p><ol><li><strong>Nature and authorisation: </strong>when you start a plan, you authorise KARMICARE (through our payment processor, Stripe) to charge your chosen payment method automatically at your replenishment interval (for example every 30, 60 or 90 days).</li><li><strong>No minimum lock-in: </strong>plans have no mandatory minimum period. You can change or end your plan at any time.</li><li><strong>Customer portal: </strong>you manage your plan in your self-service <a href=\"https://checkout.karmicare.com/a/loop_subscriptions/customer\" target=\"_blank\">customer portal</a>, where you can at any time skip an upcoming delivery, pause your plan for a period you choose, change your delivery frequency, update your shipping address or payment details, or cancel your plan entirely.</li><li><strong>Renewal reminders and cut-off: </strong>we email you <strong>3 to 5 days before </strong>every renewal charge. Changes, skips and cancellations must be made at least <strong>24 hours before</strong> the renewal billing date to stop that order.</li><li><strong>Price changes:</strong> if we change the recurring price of a plan, we give you at least <strong>30 calendar days’ notice</strong> by email. If you do not accept the new price, you can cancel before it takes effect.</li><li><strong>60-day satisfaction guarantee:</strong> as set out in clause 4.2, your first order on the 60-Day plan or the Karmicare Year is covered by the 60-day satisfaction guarantee, with a 100% refund to your original payment method if you are not satisfied.</li></ol>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_at3pLy": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Force majeure",
            "title": "Clause 10 – Force majeure",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>If something truly beyond anyone’s control blocks the contract for more than 30 days, either of us can end it and you get your money back.</strong></p><ol><li>Neither party is liable for delay or failure caused by force majeure (Article 5.226 of the Belgian Civil Code): an event beyond reasonable control that is unforeseeable, unavoidable and makes performance temporarily or permanently impossible (for example natural disasters, armed conflict, government restrictions, severe disruption of telecom or power networks, pandemic travel bans or general postal strikes).</li><li>During force majeure, our obligations are suspended. If it lasts more than <strong>30 consecutive days</strong>, either party may end the contract with immediate effect by written notice, and all prepaid amounts for undelivered goods are refunded within 14 calendar days without further compensation.</li></ol>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_qyyKHX": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Reviews and use",
            "title": "Clause 11 – Intellectual property",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>The Karmicare name, formulas, designs and content belong to KARMICA BV.</strong></p><ol><li>All elements of the KARMICARE brand, website and range, including the name “KARMICARE”, trademarks, logos, proprietary cosmetic formulations, packaging designs, airless pump concepts, photographs, graphics, text, videos, scripts and educational content, are the exclusive intellectual property of KARMICA BV or its licensors and are protected by copyright, trademark and design law.</li><li>Any reproduction, distribution, imitation, commercial use, decompilation or reverse engineering of KARMICARE intellectual property without our prior written permission is prohibited.</li></ol>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_pjNTAq": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Complaints and law",
            "title": "Clause 12 – Reviews and acceptable use",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Every review comes from a verified order, and the site is for lawful use only.</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Review authenticity:</strong> reviews published on <a href=\"https://www.karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">karmicare.com</a> are collected only from verified purchasers, through automated verification after delivery. We do not publish incentivised, fake or sponsored reviews presented as organic feedback.</li><li><strong>Acceptable use: </strong>you agree to use our website and customer portal only for lawful purposes and in line with these Terms. Automated scraping, data harvesting, malicious code or interference with checkout is prohibited.</li></ol>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        },
        "content_section_m4qTXH": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Withdrawal form",
            "title": "Clause 13 – Complaints, applicable law and courts",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Write to us first. If we cannot agree, independent mediation is available, and the consumer law of your own country still protects you.</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Complaints:</strong> for questions, feedback or complaints about our formulas or services, write to our customer care at <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a>. We acknowledge your complaint within 24 hours and give a substantiated answer or solution within <strong>seven (7) business days.</strong></li><li><strong>Out-of-court dispute resolution:</strong> if we cannot reach an amicable solution, European consumers can turn to independent consumer mediation: the <strong>Belgian Consumer Mediation Service</strong> (Consumentenombudsdienst / Service de Médiation pour le Consommateur), North Gate II, Boulevard du Roi Albert II 8, box 1, 1000 Brussels · Tel. +32 2 702 52 00 · <a href=\"mailto:contact@consumentenombudsdienst.be\" target=\"_blank\">contact@consumentenombudsdienst.be</a> · <a href=\"https://consumerombudsman.be/en\" target=\"_blank\">consumerombudsman.be/en</a>. For a dispute across EU borders, the European Consumer Centre in your country can help; in Belgium: European Consumer Centre Belgium, Koning Albert II-laan 16, 1000 Brussels · Tel. +32 2 277 99 00 · <a href=\"mailto:info@eccbelgium.be\" target=\"_blank\">info@eccbelgium.be</a>.</li><li><strong>Applicable law:</strong> all agreements between KARMICA BV and its customers are governed by <strong>Belgian law</strong>. Under <strong>Article 6 of Regulation (EC) No 593/2008 (“Rome I”),</strong> this choice does not deprive a consumer living in another EU Member State or the United Kingdom of the protection of the mandatory provisions of the law of their country of habitual residence.</li><li><strong>Competent courts:</strong> for consumers domiciled in the European Union, the jurisdiction rules of the <strong>Brussels I bis Regulation (EU) No 1215/2012</strong> apply: you may bring proceedings before the Belgian courts or the competent courts of the Member State where you live. For B2B purchasers or parties domiciled outside the EEA and the UK, the Enterprise Court of Ghent, division Bruges, has exclusive jurisdiction.</li></ol>",
            "block_content": ""
          }
        }
      },
